From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 13:14:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733: Add the hardware spinlock

The A733 has a hardware spinlock unit with 32 locks at 0x03005000,
shared between the Arm cores and the E902 companion core (A733
manual, 6.2.1, 6.2.5). Its bus gate and reset are in SPINLOCK_BGR_REG
(4.1.6.87). Add the node. The unit has an interrupt (SPI 105), which
the binding does not describe and the driver does not use.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: the driver binds and reports 32 locks; lock 0
is taken by a read of 0 and freed by a write of 0.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
index d520847695b2..b0473c959c7f 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
@@ -1046,6 +1046,15 @@ spi1: spi@2541000 {
 			#size-cells = <0>;
 		};
 
+		hwlock: hwlock@3005000 {
+			compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-hwspinlock",
+				     "allwinner,sun6i-a31-hwspinlock";
+			reg = <0x03005000 0x1000>;
+			clocks = <&ccu CLK_BUS_SPINLOCK>;
+			resets = <&ccu RST_BUS_SPINLOCK>;
+			#hwlock-cells = <1>;
+		};
+
 		sid: efuse@3006000 {
 			compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-sid",
 				     "allwinner,sun50i-a64-sid";
